(2081283, 285700, 17507, '<td valign="top">one of the few I''ve seen so far w/o the artist''s name in the title - that can actually get away without the reference by name. Subject-wise, I have to say I''m not a fan of shots that focus primarily on figurines... I feel like it''s kind of like taking a macro  of a dollar bill. In this case, it''s like a macro of a dollar bill in a jar of urine. (Were you faithful to your title?) <br/> <br/>The original photo derived a lot of its power from its sanguine color and careful use of texture and light - not to mention that it''s a <i>crucifix with the hanging body of Christ</i> in a jar of piss. No angel can equal the impact of the Son of God for impact in this context.<br/> <br/>I wonder what you learned while making this picture.<br/> <br/> <br/>Aside from those two points, one of which is definitely personal bias and the other of which may be needlessly comparative, I think this is a good picture. There''s enough detail to hold interest - and a well-placed highlight on the halo - with enough obscured to create a sense of depth and mystery. The diffuse lighting through the liquid creates an eerie glowing effect around the figurine. It will be interesting to see how this one scores.</td>', 'one of the few I''ve seen so far w/o the artist''s name in the title - that can actually get away without the reference by name. Subject-wise, I have to say I''m not a fan of shots that focus primarily on figurines... I feel like it''s kind of like taking a macro  of a dollar bill. In this case, it''s like a macro of a dollar bill in a jar of urine. (Were you faithful to your title?)  The original photo derived a lot of its power from its sanguine color and careful use of texture and light - not to mention that it''s a crucifix with the hanging body of Christ in a jar of piss. No angel can equal the impact of the Son of God for impact in this context. I wonder what you learned while making this picture.  Aside from those two points, one of which is definitely personal bias and the other of which may be needlessly comparative, I think this is a good picture. There''s enough detail to hold interest - and a well-placed highlight on the halo - with enough obscured to create a sense of depth and mystery. The diffuse lighting through the liquid creates an eerie glowing effect around the figurine. It will be interesting to see how this one scores.', '2006-01-25 04:05:59.000000', NULL, 1),
