(2084467, 285492, 15768, '<td valign="top">Damn that''s a great shot Graphicfunk! <br/>I had a similar idea a while back with different electronic components exposed under the skin and stuff, but never thought I could pull it off. Nice job!</td>', 'Damn that''s a great shot Graphicfunk! I had a similar idea a while back with different electronic components exposed under the skin and stuff, but never thought I could pull it off. Nice job!', '2006-01-25 19:34:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(2084481, 285341, 18197, '<td valign="top">Part of the fun of the challenge is comparing the photos to the work of the photographers they''re paying tribute to. I can''t figure out who that would be in this case. Still a worthy photo. The background is a bit noisy and the subject a bit sharp. You may have intended this look but it would not be my preference.</td>', 'Part of the fun of the challenge is comparing the photos to the work of the photographers they''re paying tribute to. I can''t figure out who that would be in this case. Still a worthy photo. The background is a bit noisy and the subject a bit sharp. You may have intended this look but it would not be my preference.', '2006-01-25 19:39:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2084492, 284882, 18197, '<td valign="top">Part of the fun of the challenge is comparing the photos to the work of the photographers they''re paying tribute to. I can''t figure out who that would be in this case. I am not too fond of abstacts so my reaction to this might be a bit pre-ordained. It feels to me that the centered composition would be less interesting than an off centered one consistent with the golden mean / rule of thirds. Now you may have intentionally centered the composition, and that''s fine, but it wouldn''t be my preference.</td>', 'Part of the fun of the challenge is comparing the photos to the work of the photographers they''re paying tribute to. I can''t figure out who that would be in this case. I am not too fond of abstacts so my reaction to this might be a bit pre-ordained. It feels to me that the centered composition would be less interesting than an off centered one consistent with the golden mean / rule of thirds. Now you may have intentionally centered the composition, and that''s fine, but it wouldn''t be my preference.', '2006-01-25 19:42:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2084495, 285602, 37818, '<td valign="top">FOr me this is so close to great...I have a problem with the eyes...it looks as if ther has been some odd burning ... and I have no idea who you are emulating...But a lovely shot none the less</td>', 'FOr me this is so close to great...I have a problem with the eyes...it looks as if ther has been some odd burning ... and I have no idea who you are emulating...But a lovely shot none the less', '2006-01-25 19:42:42.000000', NULL, 1),
