(2088564, 284923, 50216, '<td valign="top">Similar to Ansel, but the twigs and clutter at the bottom detract and seem less clean.</td>', 'Similar to Ansel, but the twigs and clutter at the bottom detract and seem less clean.', '2006-01-26 14:59:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(2088568, 285747, 50216, '<td valign="top">Nice!  I like the lighting just around the right eye.</td>', 'Nice!  I like the lighting just around the right eye.', '2006-01-26 15:00:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2088653, 283583, 37893, '<td valign="top">I am glad that this is reminiscent of John''s work. The colors and saturations leaves me breathless as I remember seeing one of his pieces in a Colorado Gallery a few years back. This reminds me much of his "fall collection". Great tribute I am sure he will truly love and appreciate.</td>', 'I am glad that this is reminiscent of John''s work. The colors and saturations leaves me breathless as I remember seeing one of his pieces in a Colorado Gallery a few years back. This reminds me much of his "fall collection". Great tribute I am sure he will truly love and appreciate.', '2006-01-26 15:23:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2088674, 285672, 37893, '<td valign="top">I like the use duotones for this image in tribute to Kerik. Although kerik''s approach to duotones is slightly more muted (less reds), I do appreciate the quality and style that you adapted to make it your own. One of Kerik''s known qualities is the almost soft yet sharp images. In my opinion, this might be too sharp as seen in the halos around the smaller branches. However, this image still leaves me with thoughts of mystery and drama that I am sure will be applauded by most. Great work my friend.</td>', 'I like the use duotones for this image in tribute to Kerik. Although kerik''s approach to duotones is slightly more muted (less reds), I do appreciate the quality and style that you adapted to make it your own. One of Kerik''s known qualities is the almost soft yet sharp images. In my opinion, this might be too sharp as seen in the halos around the smaller branches. However, this image still leaves me with thoughts of mystery and drama that I am sure will be applauded by most. Great work my friend.', '2006-01-26 15:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(2088682, 285241, 37893, '<td valign="top">When Adams''s didn''t have dark, strong, angry clouds, he had gradiated skies from dark to light. It is this type of sky that I see in this composition. Small yet still effective. The tonal qualities of this image is striking and the use of a wide angle completes this spot on tribute to one of our greatest photographers. Great job!</td>', 'When Adams''s didn''t have dark, strong, angry clouds, he had gradiated skies from dark to light. It is this type of sky that I see in this composition. Small yet still effective. The tonal qualities of this image is striking and the use of a wide angle completes this spot on tribute to one of our greatest photographers. Great job!', '2006-01-26 15:28:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2088695, 285675, 37893, '<td valign="top">Gradiated skies to replace dark angry clouds is what Adams has also been known for. I like how you adjusted the polarizer in such a way that the gradiations start from the left. Although it leaves me to wonder how this image would look like had it been gradiated from top down. The wide expanse of the space is truly outstanding and I''m glad you used a wide angle to capture these gentle footsteps in the snow. Great job!</td>', 'Gradiated skies to replace dark angry clouds is what Adams has also been known for. I like how you adjusted the polarizer in such a way that the gradiations start from the left. Although it leaves me to wonder how this image would look like had it been gradiated from top down. The wide expanse of the space is truly outstanding and I''m glad you used a wide angle to capture these gentle footsteps in the snow. Great job!', '2006-01-26 15:30:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2088697, 284196, 38234, '<td valign="top">excellent!!</td>', 'excellent!!', '2006-01-26 15:30:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2088705, 285492, 17850, '<td valign="top">This is one of the best photos of this challenge. I would be surprised if it will not be placed in top three. Congratulations! (10)</td>', 'This is one of the best photos of this challenge. I would be surprised if it will not be placed in top three. Congratulations! (10)', '2006-01-26 15:32:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(2088713, 284595, 37893, '<td valign="top">A nice nostalgic feeling to this image in perfect tribute to Mr. Bailey. I was not familiar with his work and thanks to you, I have him bookmarked as one of many photographers I will try to emulate. The use of the old feel frame in this image is spot on as Bailey does. However, bailey seems to be known for also burning the edges of his images (a point not taken away from you). I like this image. Maybe a bit of burn in the sky to bring out some shadows would make this image even further stand out. Great job my friend.</td>', 'A nice nostalgic feeling to this image in perfect tribute to Mr. Bailey. I was not familiar with his work and thanks to you, I have him bookmarked as one of many photographers I will try to emulate. The use of the old feel frame in this image is spot on as Bailey does. However, bailey seems to be known for also burning the edges of his images (a point not taken away from you). I like this image. Maybe a bit of burn in the sky to bring out some shadows would make this image even further stand out. Great job my friend.', '2006-01-26 15:33:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(2088733, 285363, 37893, '<td valign="top">the use of sepia to portray this lovely old soul is highly effective. There seems to be so many stories behind those eyes of which I know has seen and experienced a lot in life. Might I suggest that the slight graiation in the border be taken out? It''s slightly distracting in my honest opinion. Great job!</td>', 'the use of sepia to portray this lovely old soul is highly effective. There seems to be so many stories behind those eyes of which I know has seen and experienced a lot in life. Might I suggest that the slight graiation in the border be taken out? It''s slightly distracting in my honest opinion. Great job!', '2006-01-26 15:37:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(2088735, 285425, 14620, '<td valign="top">I see your tribute in every inch of this photograph.  Well done!</td>', 'I see your tribute in every inch of this photograph.  Well done!', '2006-01-26 15:37:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2088743, 285602, 37893, '<td valign="top">I love this portrait. The shallow DOF used in this image truly enhances and emphasizes her eyes that are just utterly stunning and sharp. Lovely model and great 3/4 angle of your POV. Great job!<br/> <br/>Edit to add: Into my faves ;)</td>', 'I love this portrait. The shallow DOF used in this image truly enhances and emphasizes her eyes that are just utterly stunning and sharp. Lovely model and great 3/4 angle of your POV. Great job! Edit to add: Into my faves ;)', '2006-01-26 15:39:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2088745, 284836, 38234, '<td valign="top">nicely done - they''d BOTH be proud!!</td>', 'nicely done - they''d BOTH be proud!!', '2006-01-26 15:39:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(2088765, 285211, 37893, '<td valign="top">I like the tonal qualities of this image. It took me a second to put everything in place and caught me by surprise but what a pleasant surprise it was. I love the curves of this old tree (driftwood). As a suggestion, maybe if you burned the rocks a slight bit as well as the wood, you can really make this image sing ;) Great job!</td>', 'I like the tonal qualities of this image. It took me a second to put everything in place and caught me by surprise but what a pleasant surprise it was. I love the curves of this old tree (driftwood). As a suggestion, maybe if you burned the rocks a slight bit as well as the wood, you can really make this image sing ;) Great job!', '2006-01-26 15:45:19.000000', NULL, 1),
