(2096263, 285423, 37893, '<td valign="top">This is a nice capture. Solid on the foundation of BW that Ansel would use. I would suggest locating the peaks since it''s your main subject in the thirds using ROTs. This would make for a stronger image IMHO. Great shot!</td>', 'This is a nice capture. Solid on the foundation of BW that Ansel would use. I would suggest locating the peaks since it''s your main subject in the thirds using ROTs. This would make for a stronger image IMHO. Great shot!', '2006-01-28 21:38:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(2096268, 285338, 37893, '<td valign="top">I knew someone would do Librodo. While the scarf and the crop are definitely Librodo, I believe Manny uses color and texture to exemplify his master and skill in portrait photography. I see the image and it leaves me wondering for more. However, I believe that this challenge should also be a direct representation of the photographer (you).  I like it and it would make for a great photo for your child to cherish someday ;) My only suggestion would be to leave some space by the corner of the left eye and the scarf ;) Great job! 7</td>', 'I knew someone would do Librodo. While the scarf and the crop are definitely Librodo, I believe Manny uses color and texture to exemplify his master and skill in portrait photography. I see the image and it leaves me wondering for more. However, I believe that this challenge should also be a direct representation of the photographer (you).  I like it and it would make for a great photo for your child to cherish someday ;) My only suggestion would be to leave some space by the corner of the left eye and the scarf ;) Great job! 7', '2006-01-28 21:40:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(2096278, 283475, 37893, '<td valign="top">Ahhh Warhol and his psychedelic colors. This to me looks good but has definite room for improvement. As a suggestion, maybe the photo was taken from a different vantage point. From up above for example so you are looking down at the shoes and the shoes are all arranged in an orderly manner. The coloration is great and I think it best reflects Warhol''s art pieces but the "haphazard" positioning of the shoes leaves little interest to hold you viewer to pause and take in the image as a whole composition. My opinion of course ;)</td>', 'Ahhh Warhol and his psychedelic colors. This to me looks good but has definite room for improvement. As a suggestion, maybe the photo was taken from a different vantage point. From up above for example so you are looking down at the shoes and the shoes are all arranged in an orderly manner. The coloration is great and I think it best reflects Warhol''s art pieces but the "haphazard" positioning of the shoes leaves little interest to hold you viewer to pause and take in the image as a whole composition. My opinion of course ;)', '2006-01-28 21:43:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2096281, 285283, 37893, '<td valign="top">Nice BW image with stark and absolute contrasts. A few things to look at would be the window on the top left corner. This doesn''t really add anything to the image so I suggest it cropped out. The bottom of the windows seem a bit dark even on my bright monitor. I suspect that most people would comment on this particular area. I think the layers and textures of this image holds enough merit that you will score great in this challenge. Good job!</td>', 'Nice BW image with stark and absolute contrasts. A few things to look at would be the window on the top left corner. This doesn''t really add anything to the image so I suggest it cropped out. The bottom of the windows seem a bit dark even on my bright monitor. I suspect that most people would comment on this particular area. I think the layers and textures of this image holds enough merit that you will score great in this challenge. Good job!', '2006-01-28 21:45:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2096285, 285631, 37893, '<td valign="top">I think the intention here is to show something that is derlichte and in a state of abandonment. I think the position of the bech is a bit awkward as it''s just simply a straight and head on elevation of it. Had it been shot from a different angle, I think this would score fairly well. Please don''t take this the wrong way but there seems to be little interest that makes wme want to look and come back at this image. I am leaving you comments because I think it is something that you would benefit from. My opinions of course.</td>', 'I think the intention here is to show something that is derlichte and in a state of abandonment. I think the position of the bech is a bit awkward as it''s just simply a straight and head on elevation of it. Had it been shot from a different angle, I think this would score fairly well. Please don''t take this the wrong way but there seems to be little interest that makes wme want to look and come back at this image. I am leaving you comments because I think it is something that you would benefit from. My opinions of course.', '2006-01-28 21:47:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2096289, 285738, 37893, '<td valign="top">You got it! Great shot and POV.<br/> <br/>edit to add: actually it''s pretty damn good ;)</td>', 'You got it! Great shot and POV. edit to add: actually it''s pretty damn good ;)', '2006-01-28 21:48:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(2096294, 284692, 37893, '<td valign="top">Great overall image. the placement and location of the plow it seems is spot on and follows the ROTs down to the tee! I like the pureness of this image and aside from a clone of that small brush to the left of the plow, I wouldb''t change a thing. 7</td>', 'Great overall image. the placement and location of the plow it seems is spot on and follows the ROTs down to the tee! I like the pureness of this image and aside from a clone of that small brush to the left of the plow, I wouldb''t change a thing. 7', '2006-01-28 21:49:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(2096306, 285287, 37893, '<td valign="top">If this would be for the infamous DrJones then I would suggest a bit more cleavage and seduction ;) The reflections of the lights and the cords on the martini shaker is a bit distracting and you could actually see yourself in the shot ;) I would say, more cleavage and show both busoms if you could and this would be a DrJones entry alright! Great work! 6</td>', 'If this would be for the infamous DrJones then I would suggest a bit more cleavage and seduction ;) The reflections of the lights and the cords on the martini shaker is a bit distracting and you could actually see yourself in the shot ;) I would say, more cleavage and show both busoms if you could and this would be a DrJones entry alright! Great work! 6', '2006-01-28 21:51:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(2096310, 285341, 37893, '<td valign="top">The image grain of this photo seems to compliment the emotion that is being shown here. I think the image in itself is great and the look in his eyes are wonderful. I would have probably had him not in the center but to the left of the frame to follow the ROTs. Great work. 6</td>', 'The image grain of this photo seems to compliment the emotion that is being shown here. I think the image in itself is great and the look in his eyes are wonderful. I would have probably had him not in the center but to the left of the frame to follow the ROTs. Great work. 6', '2006-01-28 21:52:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(2096314, 283278, 37893, '<td valign="top">This is a nice view of this City that i haven''t seen before. I think the brush in the foreground while there for scale and definition, seems a bit distracting. The placement of the skyline is great although the horizon seems like it wants to be lower so as not to cut the image in half. A bit of burn in the clouds and I think you have a great tribute image here. Great work my friend. 7</td>', 'This is a nice view of this City that i haven''t seen before. I think the brush in the foreground while there for scale and definition, seems a bit distracting. The placement of the skyline is great although the horizon seems like it wants to be lower so as not to cut the image in half. A bit of burn in the clouds and I think you have a great tribute image here. Great work my friend. 7', '2006-01-28 21:54:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(2096320, 285758, 37893, '<td valign="top">The beauty of Weston''s work is that he photographs the most mundane objects and makes them sing through his visions and use of BW. This might be one of them with a few tweaks to the image. I think a landscape crop instead of a portrait crop would have been better and a wider frame stroke would captivate this image even further. But I do like your boldness of selecting this photographer. It''s tough to tribute something to him and I think you;ve done a great job but it could be pushed a bit further. Great work. 6</td>', 'The beauty of Weston''s work is that he photographs the most mundane objects and makes them sing through his visions and use of BW. This might be one of them with a few tweaks to the image. I think a landscape crop instead of a portrait crop would have been better and a wider frame stroke would captivate this image even further. But I do like your boldness of selecting this photographer. It''s tough to tribute something to him and I think you;ve done a great job but it could be pushed a bit further. Great work. 6', '2006-01-28 21:56:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(2096451, 285575, 48228, '<td valign="top">I loved this thumbnail and I really love it when blown up. You have certainly captured Picasso brilliantly....."WOW" factor here for sure.</td>', 'I loved this thumbnail and I really love it when blown up. You have certainly captured Picasso brilliantly....."WOW" factor here for sure.', '2006-01-28 22:32:28.000000', NULL, 1),
