(2103829, 284688, 48865, '<td valign="top">Very cool, wondering how you did it.....hmmmmmmm.</td>', 'Very cool, wondering how you did it.....hmmmmmmm.', '2006-01-30 21:56:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103838, 285213, 37893, '<td valign="top">Hello Rae-Ann. The use of duotones for this image is effective yet still lacks the Leibovitz touch IMHO. I think BW would have been better. Maggie''s eyes, while piercing and quite striking, seems a bit overdone. I think the crop could have been improved on this image as well. Cut off hands and knuckles adds up in terms of what the viewer is looking for. Of course, these are all my opinion, and honest ones at that, so just take it with a grain of salt and keep the good ones and ditch the bad ones ;)</td>', 'Hello Rae-Ann. The use of duotones for this image is effective yet still lacks the Leibovitz touch IMHO. I think BW would have been better. Maggie''s eyes, while piercing and quite striking, seems a bit overdone. I think the crop could have been improved on this image as well. Cut off hands and knuckles adds up in terms of what the viewer is looking for. Of course, these are all my opinion, and honest ones at that, so just take it with a grain of salt and keep the good ones and ditch the bad ones ;)', '2006-01-30 22:01:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103900, 285394, 37893, '<td valign="top">Nice tight crop that is a great sentimental photo as well. The BW sure is Leibovitz ;) I just wish the ear wasn''t in the crop. Go tighter I say ;) Great job!</td>', 'Nice tight crop that is a great sentimental photo as well. The BW sure is Leibovitz ;) I just wish the ear wasn''t in the crop. Go tighter I say ;) Great job!', '2006-01-30 22:31:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103902, 284882, 37893, '<td valign="top">This I''m positive will suffer DPC votings. Abstracts unfortunately don''t do so well here. I''ve done a few and it wasn''t where I expected the scores to be ;( An improvement perhaps would be to locate the flower itself usig ROTs. It''s amazing how many entries actually forget about this most basic rule in photography ;) I hope you do well and meet your goals in thie challenge. Good luck my friend.</td>', 'This I''m positive will suffer DPC votings. Abstracts unfortunately don''t do so well here. I''ve done a few and it wasn''t where I expected the scores to be ;( An improvement perhaps would be to locate the flower itself usig ROTs. It''s amazing how many entries actually forget about this most basic rule in photography ;) I hope you do well and meet your goals in thie challenge. Good luck my friend.', '2006-01-30 22:33:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103907, 283584, 37893, '<td valign="top">Helmut Newton typifies sex and BW photography. I think there is a bit of "sex" in this image by the use of just a tiny fold in her skirt. It makes your voters kinda wonder as skin is shown through. I think the shoes would have been better if they were solid and not patterned. Some hot spots and blown highlights might eventually hurt your score in this challenge. Good luck.</td>', 'Helmut Newton typifies sex and BW photography. I think there is a bit of "sex" in this image by the use of just a tiny fold in her skirt. It makes your voters kinda wonder as skin is shown through. I think the shoes would have been better if they were solid and not patterned. Some hot spots and blown highlights might eventually hurt your score in this challenge. Good luck.', '2006-01-30 22:34:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103910, 285081, 37893, '<td valign="top">Hmmm quite interesting but I think this will fall under the radar in voting. The mix of colors are nice as are the textures of the bubbles but nothing seems to really hold the composition together. Sorry just my honest opinion.</td>', 'Hmmm quite interesting but I think this will fall under the radar in voting. The mix of colors are nice as are the textures of the bubbles but nothing seems to really hold the composition together. Sorry just my honest opinion.', '2006-01-30 22:34:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103916, 284118, 37893, '<td valign="top">The sky is eeriely smooth and soft at the same time. This might have turned out better had that foreign object in front weren''t there. Where is this structure located? Great shot though then again, I love architecture ;)</td>', 'The sky is eeriely smooth and soft at the same time. This might have turned out better had that foreign object in front weren''t there. Where is this structure located? Great shot though then again, I love architecture ;)', '2006-01-30 22:36:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103922, 285725, 37893, '<td valign="top">The noise and artifacting shows in my monitor specially underneath where the shades and shadows are founf. Compositionally, it''s almost split in the middle. I would probably shift the weiner so that it''s not centrally composed. I hope that makes sense.</td>', 'The noise and artifacting shows in my monitor specially underneath where the shades and shadows are founf. Compositionally, it''s almost split in the middle. I would probably shift the weiner so that it''s not centrally composed. I hope that makes sense.', '2006-01-30 22:37:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103942, 285726, 37893, '<td valign="top">I think this is a perfect take on Hine''s imagery :) The horizon is aligned correctly and the subject is properly placed within ROTs. The contrast between the snow and the sky is absolute and I like it. Great job! 7</td>', 'I think this is a perfect take on Hine''s imagery :) The horizon is aligned correctly and the subject is properly placed within ROTs. The contrast between the snow and the sky is absolute and I like it. Great job! 7', '2006-01-30 22:48:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103943, 285482, 37893, '<td valign="top">The focus on this image is dead on! Amazing how the veins of the leaves are clearly shown and the background blur is just right ;) The leaf to the upper left could have been clones out as it doesn''t really add much to the image IMHO. Great job!</td>', 'The focus on this image is dead on! Amazing how the veins of the leaves are clearly shown and the background blur is just right ;) The leaf to the upper left could have been clones out as it doesn''t really add much to the image IMHO. Great job!', '2006-01-30 22:49:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103947, 284891, 37893, '<td valign="top">Back for comments. I saw the thumbnail and first reaction was WOW! But then when I clicked on the larger version, the image seems a bit soft. The grandeur of Al Capitan is clearly shown in this image. The crop could have been tighter so that the verticality of this massive granite face could clearly come across.</td>', 'Back for comments. I saw the thumbnail and first reaction was WOW! But then when I clicked on the larger version, the image seems a bit soft. The grandeur of Al Capitan is clearly shown in this image. The crop could have been tighter so that the verticality of this massive granite face could clearly come across.', '2006-01-30 22:50:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103952, 284867, 37893, '<td valign="top">Ansel was not really known for architecture images however, he was known for absolute skies. in this case, the use of the polarizer created this effect and kudos to you. Perspective correction might could have been applied to this challenge. I believe it would do wonders as the verticals have a slight tilt to them due to parallax. I would clone out the tree in the right as it doesn''t really do much for this image IMHO.</td>', 'Ansel was not really known for architecture images however, he was known for absolute skies. in this case, the use of the polarizer created this effect and kudos to you. Perspective correction might could have been applied to this challenge. I believe it would do wonders as the verticals have a slight tilt to them due to parallax. I would clone out the tree in the right as it doesn''t really do much for this image IMHO.', '2006-01-30 22:52:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103971, 285655, 37893, '<td valign="top">The use of leading lines in this image is spot on and highly effective. As my eye is drawn into the photo, alas, there is a figure just to the horizon to stop me from going any further. The snow seems a bit gray though. Since we could clone out items, I would have probably cloned out the drain on the right of the road. This would really emphasize the road and it''s distinct features. I would also remove the dark area to the bottom right of the image ;) Great job though and a bit of a boost in curves would really make this image a great one! Great shot my friend.</td>', 'The use of leading lines in this image is spot on and highly effective. As my eye is drawn into the photo, alas, there is a figure just to the horizon to stop me from going any further. The snow seems a bit gray though. Since we could clone out items, I would have probably cloned out the drain on the right of the road. This would really emphasize the road and it''s distinct features. I would also remove the dark area to the bottom right of the image ;) Great job though and a bit of a boost in curves would really make this image a great one! Great shot my friend.', '2006-01-30 23:02:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103975, 285345, 37893, '<td valign="top">The image is soft in many respects but the desat works well in employing a very somber feeling to this image. Her pose captures IMHO the essence of Doisneau''s images ;) Great shot and great candid.</td>', 'The image is soft in many respects but the desat works well in employing a very somber feeling to this image. Her pose captures IMHO the essence of Doisneau''s images ;) Great shot and great candid.', '2006-01-30 23:03:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103978, 285639, 37893, '<td valign="top">I believe this one has way too many distractions. I do realize that shooting between the trees is a tough mark but the branches just becomes too overbearing at times. Maybe if the background was a lot simpler, then the branches would stand out on their own. Just my opinion of course ;)</td>', 'I believe this one has way too many distractions. I do realize that shooting between the trees is a tough mark but the branches just becomes too overbearing at times. Maybe if the background was a lot simpler, then the branches would stand out on their own. Just my opinion of course ;)', '2006-01-30 23:05:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103983, 283710, 37893, '<td valign="top">Great long exposure here. I think the blue skies in the background is just a tad saturated and takes away from the main subjects and focus of this image. However, the trickery used to make the King disappear might revel well with the voters. Great shot.</td>', 'Great long exposure here. I think the blue skies in the background is just a tad saturated and takes away from the main subjects and focus of this image. However, the trickery used to make the King disappear might revel well with the voters. Great shot.', '2006-01-30 23:07:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103987, 285627, 37893, '<td valign="top">Lovely tribute to Parks. I neveer heard of him before but thanks to you, he is now part of my bookmarked collections of photographers ;) The focus here is soft but works well IMHO. the texture of the background, while light, is a bit distracting on the left hand side. The sahdow definition is indeed captivating and "alluring". It leaves me to wonder, what happened to the left strap of her dress ;) I know, details details ;) Great job my friend ;)</td>', 'Lovely tribute to Parks. I neveer heard of him before but thanks to you, he is now part of my bookmarked collections of photographers ;) The focus here is soft but works well IMHO. the texture of the background, while light, is a bit distracting on the left hand side. The sahdow definition is indeed captivating and "alluring". It leaves me to wonder, what happened to the left strap of her dress ;) I know, details details ;) Great job my friend ;)', '2006-01-30 23:09:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(2103993, 284589, 37893, '<td valign="top">Very nice. Eventhough Gibson was known for BWs, I think your take on his style is good. A sense of balance might be achieved had the lady in heels on the upper right had the same foot pose as the one on the left and the center guy was, well, centered ;) A bit grainy for my taste but a sure definition of Gibson''s work ;) Great job!</td>', 'Very nice. Eventhough Gibson was known for BWs, I think your take on his style is good. A sense of balance might be achieved had the lady in heels on the upper right had the same foot pose as the one on the left and the center guy was, well, centered ;) A bit grainy for my taste but a sure definition of Gibson''s work ;) Great job!', '2006-01-30 23:11:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(2104007, 283454, 37893, '<td valign="top">Back for comments ;) I think this image is clean and simple with very minimal "pop" to it. Therefore I think this will finish in the middle of the pack. My suggestion to "better" the composition si to create an illusion of movement. Had the fern been placed to either the left of right with the curve going the other way, I think this would have been more effective. The softness might also be an issue with this image. A bit of USM and you''re set.</td>', 'Back for comments ;) I think this image is clean and simple with very minimal "pop" to it. Therefore I think this will finish in the middle of the pack. My suggestion to "better" the composition si to create an illusion of movement. Had the fern been placed to either the left of right with the curve going the other way, I think this would have been more effective. The softness might also be an issue with this image. A bit of USM and you''re set.', '2006-01-30 23:17:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(2104010, 283986, 37893, '<td valign="top">Landscape shots are tough IMHO. There needs to be something to captivate and allure your viewer. This image somehow leads me to look at the electric towers in the distance. There is nothing stopping my eye from roaming around the image. Maybe a dramatized sky will help improve this image. Just my opinions ;)</td>', 'Landscape shots are tough IMHO. There needs to be something to captivate and allure your viewer. This image somehow leads me to look at the electric towers in the distance. There is nothing stopping my eye from roaming around the image. Maybe a dramatized sky will help improve this image. Just my opinions ;)', '2006-01-30 23:19:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(2104011, 283895, 37893, '<td valign="top">Nice use of single light source. However the image seems to lack a bit of contrast. In my bright monitor, it''s already fairly dark and is evidenced in her face. Her look is stunning though and leads me to think what she was thinking about when you took this beautiful image. I''m sure this will be a keeper in your family for years to come.</td>', 'Nice use of single light source. However the image seems to lack a bit of contrast. In my bright monitor, it''s already fairly dark and is evidenced in her face. Her look is stunning though and leads me to think what she was thinking about when you took this beautiful image. I''m sure this will be a keeper in your family for years to come.', '2006-01-30 23:20:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2104014, 284643, 37893, '<td valign="top">Love the noise and grain in this image as well as the use of BW. I think it''s a great rendition to this photographer ;) Great job my friend.</td>', 'Love the noise and grain in this image as well as the use of BW. I think it''s a great rendition to this photographer ;) Great job my friend.', '2006-01-30 23:21:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2104016, 283852, 37893, '<td valign="top">The eyes are amazing! However, there is an object in teh foreground that impedes my view of this young boy. I am not certain what it is though at this point and I am sure you will let us know what it is. I think without it, this would have scored a bit higher for most. 6</td>', 'The eyes are amazing! However, there is an object in teh foreground that impedes my view of this young boy. I am not certain what it is though at this point and I am sure you will let us know what it is. I think without it, this would have scored a bit higher for most. 6', '2006-01-30 23:23:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2104020, 284027, 37893, '<td valign="top">Weston''s still life images are creative and effective. this has the potential to be one of them had the crop been tighter perhaps around the stem and the background smooth with no texture.</td>', 'Weston''s still life images are creative and effective. this has the potential to be one of them had the crop been tighter perhaps around the stem and the background smooth with no texture.', '2006-01-30 23:24:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2104173, 285562, 31742, '<td valign="top">Absolutely Beautiful.............10</td>', 'Absolutely Beautiful.............10', '2006-01-31 00:36:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(2104175, 285394, 31742, '<td valign="top">so0o0o cute!!</td>', 'so0o0o cute!!', '2006-01-31 00:38:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2104411, 283699, 47020, '<td valign="top">Nice shot.<br/> <br/>One thought: I haven''t studied his work enough to be certain, but I''m of the impression that "Mr. Adams" tended to use much longer shutter speeds than this must have been.  Perhaps he made exceptions, and I admit the general feel is certainly similar, but I thought I''d mention it, anyway.<br/> <br/>I still say nice shot, though.  :-)</td>', 'Nice shot. One thought: I haven''t studied his work enough to be certain, but I''m of the impression that "Mr. Adams" tended to use much longer shutter speeds than this must have been.  Perhaps he made exceptions, and I admit the general feel is certainly similar, but I thought I''d mention it, anyway. I still say nice shot, though.  :-)', '2006-01-31 03:27:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(2104422, 285341, 47020, '<td valign="top">Wow, very nice capture of this man.  I would suggest cropping a little off the top, and a fair bit (maybe 1/4 of the image) off the left (leaving a little space around his head, but cropping off a bunch of his shoulder), to frame his face more in the upper-left of the frame, for even more impact...  and that''s on a shot that I found pretty impactful to start with.  :-)<br/> <br/>Alas, the (lack of) cropping I''m finding to be more distracting than I''d like...  With it, I think this image would be at least a 9, and maybe even a 10 for me.  without it, I''m struggling... I want to give it an 8, because it''s such a nice capture of a moment, but I find it just doesn''t quite sit well with me, and so I think I''ll have to give it a 7.</td>', 'Wow, very nice capture of this man.  I would suggest cropping a little off the top, and a fair bit (maybe 1/4 of the image) off the left (leaving a little space around his head, but cropping off a bunch of his shoulder), to frame his face more in the upper-left of the frame, for even more impact...  and that''s on a shot that I found pretty impactful to start with.  :-) Alas, the (lack of) cropping I''m finding to be more distracting than I''d like...  With it, I think this image would be at least a 9, and maybe even a 10 for me.  without it, I''m struggling... I want to give it an 8, because it''s such a nice capture of a moment, but I find it just doesn''t quite sit well with me, and so I think I''ll have to give it a 7.', '2006-01-31 03:35:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2104488, 283278, 16046, '<td valign="top">Nice, this must be from that park by the medical center, I would like to go there at night sometime. Great tones.</td>', 'Nice, this must be from that park by the medical center, I would like to go there at night sometime. Great tones.', '2006-01-31 05:07:04.000000', NULL, 1),
