(2107682, 285750, 37629, '<td valign="top">thanks a lot for the great comments :) didn''t fare as well as i''d hoped in the rankings, but i''m satisfied with the score, i''ll do better next time. <br/> <br/>As for how i did it, i put a blanket on the ground, put a small chair on it with thin legs, put the camera on the ol'' tripod, set the self timer for 10 seconds, i jumped on the chair and when i heard the shutter click i held still and counted to 4 before i moved my arms. only one legs of the chair, and the tip of the other were showing, cloned that out, im lucky i had such a small chair heh.<br/> <br/>thanks again :)</td>', 'thanks a lot for the great comments :) didn''t fare as well as i''d hoped in the rankings, but i''m satisfied with the score, i''ll do better next time.  As for how i did it, i put a blanket on the ground, put a small chair on it with thin legs, put the camera on the ol'' tripod, set the self timer for 10 seconds, i jumped on the chair and when i heard the shutter click i held still and counted to 4 before i moved my arms. only one legs of the chair, and the tip of the other were showing, cloned that out, im lucky i had such a small chair heh. thanks again :)', '2006-02-01 00:32:05.000000', NULL, 0),
