(2120915, 285287, 28710, '<td valign="top">Actually, this is very reminiscent of his earlier stuff which I personally prefer over his current Glam look stuff. Compared to his work from a few years back, this is quite good.<br/> <br/>Critiques include the zipper and the fact that the martini glass isn''t quite straight...<br/> <br/>Your model has simply fantastic skin. You are one seriously lucky dude.</td>', 'Actually, this is very reminiscent of his earlier stuff which I personally prefer over his current Glam look stuff. Compared to his work from a few years back, this is quite good. Critiques include the zipper and the fact that the martini glass isn''t quite straight... Your model has simply fantastic skin. You are one seriously lucky dude.', '2006-02-04 07:17:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(2121154, 284690, 35804, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Pug-H:</b></div><hr/><i> Simple but effective. Of course, those objects wouldn''t have been so old to him (well, the book, at least, seeing he died in 1851). <br/>   I wonder what''s in your collection of Victorian photography. Do you have an on-line galery of your collection? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>I don''t have an online gallery, but that''s a really interesting idea...and a good way for me to catalog the images. A handful of images can be seen in this photograph:<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=202421" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/356/thumb/202421.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/356/thumb/202421.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_challenge/356/thumb/202421.jpg"/></a> <br/> <br/>I''d say most in my collection are portraits. I also have examples of architecture, animal, candid, and post-mortem images.</td>', 'Originally posted by Pug-H: Simple but effective. Of course, those objects wouldn''t have been so old to him (well, the book, at least, seeing he died in 1851).    I wonder what''s in your collection of Victorian photography. Do you have an on-line galery of your collection?   I don''t have an online gallery, but that''s a really interesting idea...and a good way for me to catalog the images. A handful of images can be seen in this photograph:   I''d say most in my collection are portraits. I also have examples of architecture, animal, candid, and post-mortem images.', '2006-02-04 10:05:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2121595, 285749, 11769, '<td valign="top">Another beautiful photograph.</td>', 'Another beautiful photograph.', '2006-02-04 14:19:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2121932, 285312, 52766, '<td valign="top">It''s Nice</td>', 'It''s Nice', '2006-02-04 17:35:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(2122000, 284916, 11800, '<td valign="top">I love this. It is really a wonderful study and I would have guessed Arbus right away. The title and the subject shouts out the name to anyone who has looked at her pictures. The ears, the name of the game, and the person all fit perfectly together to tell a story. And the choker is icing on the cake.<br/>Good job. Good luck on future challenges. Pay attention to the threads that run where everyone discusses their take on the challenge. They will give you pointers of what to expect in the voting.</td>', 'I love this. It is really a wonderful study and I would have guessed Arbus right away. The title and the subject shouts out the name to anyone who has looked at her pictures. The ears, the name of the game, and the person all fit perfectly together to tell a story. And the choker is icing on the cake.Good job. Good luck on future challenges. Pay attention to the threads that run where everyone discusses their take on the challenge. They will give you pointers of what to expect in the voting.', '2006-02-04 17:57:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(2122035, 285622, 11800, '<td valign="top">Did you know he built a lightbox for the street photos? That''s how he got such rich details on the subject while also getting the lovely white background. It had panels on each side and one overhead. If I remember right, the side ones were black. Maybe not. Maybe someone else improved on his idea but I think it was him. Anyway. Good job.</td>', 'Did you know he built a lightbox for the street photos? That''s how he got such rich details on the subject while also getting the lovely white background. It had panels on each side and one overhead. If I remember right, the side ones were black. Maybe not. Maybe someone else improved on his idea but I think it was him. Anyway. Good job.', '2006-02-04 18:26:00.000000', NULL, 0),
