(2809270, 285524, 46294, '<td valign="top">A great, simple picture, and a nice b/w conversion!</td>', 'A great, simple picture, and a nice b/w conversion!', '2006-09-07 07:46:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(2819437, 285196, 31403, '<td valign="top">I haven''t commented on this?  How could that be?<br/> <br/>This is cool on so many levels - loved it when I saw it in the challenge, love it still!<br/> <br/>The textures are just - hmm - it''s like I can taste them!  It''s beyond being able to feel them, it''s like an expereience - the repetition in the composition, the beautiful curves of the lamp base (not once but twice) - the texture in the lamp shade - how do you get texture in a lamp shade?  Mine tend to just blow out!<br/> <br/>Really it''s kind of beyond my ability to express how this makes me feel - hopefully that gives you at least an idea of how cool I think this is.<br/> <br/>I think it comes down to the magic of photography being so manifest here.  It''s a simple scene, could be any house (although it feels kind of retro so it calls upon memories I didn''t know I had) but photography turns this simple scene into something that calls up all this emotion.  Isn''t that just magic?  <br/> <br/>Great work!  To say the least -</td>', 'I haven''t commented on this?  How could that be? This is cool on so many levels - loved it when I saw it in the challenge, love it still! The textures are just - hmm - it''s like I can taste them!  It''s beyond being able to feel them, it''s like an expereience - the repetition in the composition, the beautiful curves of the lamp base (not once but twice) - the texture in the lamp shade - how do you get texture in a lamp shade?  Mine tend to just blow out! Really it''s kind of beyond my ability to express how this makes me feel - hopefully that gives you at least an idea of how cool I think this is. I think it comes down to the magic of photography being so manifest here.  It''s a simple scene, could be any house (although it feels kind of retro so it calls upon memories I didn''t know I had) but photography turns this simple scene into something that calls up all this emotion.  Isn''t that just magic?   Great work!  To say the least -', '2006-09-10 02:58:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2872051, 284864, 62812, '<td valign="top">I can see what you were trying to do here. But as for your critism of "voters" what do you expect? The whole process of voting for images is a ridiculous one in the first place and often one person''s vision may be complex and require time and a certain amount of education to appreciate as opposed to a snap judgement and a click of 4 on the mouse. The vast majority of people on here are here for fun (and posting pictures of flowers)!<br/>I havent been part of this of long and I almost began to get frustrated with the lack of originality and expression but hell its a photography competetion!<br/>Is the most popular the best or the easiest to understand?<br/>You could argue the most popular was the most ordinary as in the popular music world where the trite and anodyne rule.<br/>Anyway, looking through your pictures you have a unique vision and far from the middle of the road! And thanks for making me aware of the photography of Igor Posner.<br/>regards<br/>bood</td>', 'I can see what you were trying to do here. But as for your critism of "voters" what do you expect? The whole process of voting for images is a ridiculous one in the first place and often one person''s vision may be complex and require time and a certain amount of education to appreciate as opposed to a snap judgement and a click of 4 on the mouse. The vast majority of people on here are here for fun (and posting pictures of flowers)!I havent been part of this of long and I almost began to get frustrated with the lack of originality and expression but hell its a photography competetion!Is the most popular the best or the easiest to understand?You could argue the most popular was the most ordinary as in the popular music world where the trite and anodyne rule.Anyway, looking through your pictures you have a unique vision and far from the middle of the road! And thanks for making me aware of the photography of Igor Posner.regardsbood', '2006-09-28 09:27:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2895802, 283820, 42196, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by KaDi:</b></div><hr/><i>An interesting image of a crashing skier whose fate is uncertain.  </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Don''t think this guy is "crashing" here.<br/>He is just a sweet off-pister.</td>', 'Originally posted by KaDi:An interesting image of a crashing skier whose fate is uncertain.   Don''t think this guy is "crashing" here.He is just a sweet off-pister.', '2006-10-04 13:13:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(2895873, 283820, 55822, '<td valign="top">Wish I had seen this photo before now. How can anybody not know who Warren Miller is? This shot is fantastic, you have created a very Warren Miller scene that is truely a tribute not only to him but to your own skill in shooting a very tough shot to get. Seeing that snow is making me want snow now so i can go do this. Both actually, ski and shoot. Great shot.</td>', 'Wish I had seen this photo before now. How can anybody not know who Warren Miller is? This shot is fantastic, you have created a very Warren Miller scene that is truely a tribute not only to him but to your own skill in shooting a very tough shot to get. Seeing that snow is making me want snow now so i can go do this. Both actually, ski and shoot. Great shot.', '2006-10-04 13:35:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2912265, 285196, 46294, '<td valign="top">So simple but a great picture. The tone fits the image great!</td>', 'So simple but a great picture. The tone fits the image great!', '2006-10-09 18:31:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(2934424, 285196, 60862, '<td valign="top">Wow, Deb.  Somehow I missed this in all the times I''ve looked at your portfolio!  Great shot, very imaginative.</td>', 'Wow, Deb.  Somehow I missed this in all the times I''ve looked at your portfolio!  Great shot, very imaginative.', '2006-10-16 18:00:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2953409, 284739, 17925, '<td valign="top">i like this. looks like it came right out of a poster that talks abt street art or etc. tt smile on his face really soften e overall rough texture. great!</td>', 'i like this. looks like it came right out of a poster that talks abt street art or etc. tt smile on his face really soften e overall rough texture. great!', '2006-10-23 05:12:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2963528, 285706, 67598, '<td valign="top">you''ve tried to emulate an amazing photographer, and missed completely.. edward weston''s pepper shots show amazing tonal range, this is totally flat.  weston''s images are extremely sexual in nature, and again, this gives nothing even slightly resembling sexual form.<br/>i commend you for looking at the work of a great photographer, but using his name in your title is a bit insulting :p</td>', 'you''ve tried to emulate an amazing photographer, and missed completely.. edward weston''s pepper shots show amazing tonal range, this is totally flat.  weston''s images are extremely sexual in nature, and again, this gives nothing even slightly resembling sexual form.i commend you for looking at the work of a great photographer, but using his name in your title is a bit insulting :p', '2006-10-25 22:24:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(3039222, 285196, 36470, '<td valign="top">Great idea.  I love photos that make you take a closer look.</td>', 'Great idea.  I love photos that make you take a closer look.', '2006-11-17 00:30:27.000000', NULL, 0),
